 ## Overview
-Fast Deterministic GPU Voxelization is a PyTorch-based method for converting 3D point clouds into a fixed-size voxel grid that achieves bit-identical output to a reference C++/CUDA implementation while providing a ~100x speedup [S1, unofficial]. It replaces an $O(N^2)$ sequential CUDA kernel with a parallel pipeline of filtering, coordinate computation, stable sorting, and scattering [S1, unofficial]. Unlike the standard `deterministic=False` path which relies on non-reproducible atomic operations, this method guarantees reproducibility by preserving original point order within voxels via stable sorting [S1, unofficial].
+Fast Deterministic GPU Voxelization is a PyTorch-based method for converting 3D point clouds into a fixed-size voxel grid that achieves bit-identical output to a reference C++/CUDA implementation while providing a ~100× speedup [S1, unofficial]. It replaces an $O(N^2)$ sequential CUDA kernel with a parallel pipeline of filtering, coordinate computation, stable sorting, and scattering [S1, unofficial]. Unlike the standard `deterministic=False` path which relies on non-reproducible atomic operations, this method guarantees reproducibility by preserving original point order within voxels via stable sorting [S1, unofficial].
 
